    "title": "Connally ISD Facing Possible Closure of Two Campuses - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Robert Lopez ,\n4 hours ago\nLACEY LAKEVIEW, Texas ( FOX 44 )– Texas Education Administration commissioner Mike Morath stopped into two campuses at Connally Independent School District after five consecutive years of unsatisfactory academic results.\nBoth Connally Elementary School and Connally Junior High are in a difficult situation with the TEA. The campuses have received five consecutive ‘F’ ratings from the TEA’s annual school reviews. Now the TEA must take action against the district and either appoint a new board for the campuses or possibly even shut them down.\n“He is posed with the authority to either appoint a board of directors to the district to try to solve the problem that way, or to close one of or both of the campuses,” said Michael Donaldson, director of communications at CISD.\nWhile the TEA says the district’s performance is unsatisfactory, parents in the district still believe that the schools will get better.\n“I’m confident in the things that they are doing currently and working on and working towards,” said Chris Meza, a parent at CISD. “So hopefully the state saw that as well.”\nThere is no definite timetable for the actions that the TEA will take against the district, other than Mike Morath saying it will be in the coming months.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KWKT - FOX 44.",
